    title: "The mascots carry the signs, and the children stay",
    summary: "After the luring of the children, the restaurant's mascots smell and stain. A clipping says it is threatened again with closure over a foul odor from them, and that parents report \"what appeared to be blood and mucus around the eyes and mouths of the mascots\" [[fnaf1-news-sanitation]]. It has been fighting \"an uphill battle ever since\" to bring families back [[fnaf1-news-uphill-battle]]. That these undated clippings are news of the old restaurant is the model's reading. The model reads the signs as the bodies hidden inside the four mascots, which no record shows. In one minigame the Puppet gives gifts to four grey, dead-looking children and then sets the heads of Freddy, Bonnie, Chica and Foxy on them; a fifth body is reported to show for a single frame before the yellow bear's scare [[fnaf2-give-gifts-give-life]]. The model reads the four as staying on in those four machines and the yellow bear as marking the fifth child; how that child came to it, every scene withholds. How any of them came to stay, the Cassette Man himself never learned: \"I don't know how those tiny breaths of life came to inhabit those machines.\" [[ffps-insanity-tiny-breaths]] By November 1987 the older machines smell [[fnaf2-call2-the-smell]] and, though they \"shouldn't be able to walk around\", are active from the second and third nights by a fan wiki's activity tables [[fnaf2-old-models-walk-from-night2]].",
