    title: "Fazbear's Fright finds \"a real one\"",
    summary: "\"Thirty years after Freddy Fazbear's Pizza closed it's doors\" [[scott-2015-fnaf3-store-thirty-years]], a local amusement park builds a horror attraction with relics from \"the decades-old pizzeria\" [[fnaf3-coming-soon-newspaper]]. Its builders follow a lead to \"an extra room that got boarded up\" [[fnaf3-call1-boarded-room-lead]], and the next night: \"We found one. A real one.\" [[fnaf3-call2-found-a-real-one]] The game's extras name it Springtrap [[fnaf3-springtrap-name]], and rare screens show what looks like a body inside the suit [[fnaf3-springtrap-corpse-screens]]. A hidden minigame, Happiest Day, gives six masked children a party, after which they vanish [[fnaf3-happiest-day]]; with it done, the game's last screen changes. The model tells that as the release the children were owed and the first attempt at it. It is a scene of the game and not an event fixed here: which ending happened is open [[fnaf3-bad-ending-heads]] [[fnaf3-good-ending-heads]], and Pizzeria Simulator speaks of the children as still without rest [[ffps-insanity-tiny-breaths]].",
